  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Boil the kettle. Half-fill a medium saucepan with the boiling water. Cook egg noodles in the boiling water over medium-high heat, stirring occasionally with a fork to separate, until tender, 4-5 minutes.\n• Meanwhile, cut Japanese tofu into bite-sized chunks. In a medium bowl, combine tofu, cornflour, the salt and a pinch of pepper.\n• Drain and rinse the cooked noodles.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/62f1b6be467205c7bb0c02ce/step-a60b0816.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a large frying pan, heat a generous drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat. When oil is hot, shake excess flour off tofu and cook, tossing, until browned, 3-4 minutes.\n• Transfer tofu to a paper towel-lined plate. Cover to keep warm.\n• While the tofu is cooking, thinly slice carrot and zucchini into half-moons. Roughly chop Asian greens.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/62f1b6be467205c7bb0c02ce/step-386a99b2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Wipe out frying pan, then return to high heat with a drizzle of olive oil. Cook carrot and zucchini, stirring, until tender, 4-5 minutes.\n• Add ginger paste and Asian greens and cook, stirring, until fragrant and wilted, 1-2 minutes.\n• Stir in katsu paste, coconut milk and the soy sauce. Cook until combined and heated through, 2-3 minutes.\n• Add cooked noodles, stirring, until mixed through. Remove pan from heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/62f1b6be467205c7bb0c02ce/step-1dcbb2df.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide curried egg noodles and crispy tofu between bowls.\n• Drizzle with sweet chilli sauce. Sprinkle with crispy shallots to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/62f1b6be467205c7bb0c02ce/step-a8191bbf.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
